WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.810
We've come a long way from stealing DVD players
in Los Angeles.

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:09.286
Jason Momoa, an extended family, and a sci-fi
escalation?

00:00:09.286 --> 00:00:11.672
Here's what you missed in the Fast X trailer.

00:00:11.672 --> 00:00:16.440
The new "Fast X" trailer may clock in at just
under four minutes long, but that's still

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:22.050
more than enough time for Vin Diesel's Dom
and the rest of the crew to wax poetic about

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.550
family for a while.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:28.884
All told, the word "family" is spoken on five
occasions throughout the trailer.

00:00:28.884 --> 00:00:29.384
"Family."

00:00:29.384 --> 00:00:29.890
"Family."

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:30.549
"Family."

00:00:30.549 --> 00:00:31.194
"Family"

00:00:31.194 --> 00:00:32.194
"Family."

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:36.500
That's a rate of more than one "family" per
minute, for those keeping track.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.230
All this talk of family especially tracks
with the plot of "Fast X."

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:44.160
The trailer suggests that the 10th mainline
film in the franchise is going to be more

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.070
about family than ever.

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:50.620
Dante clearly has it out for Dom on a personal
level, believing the racer to be responsible

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.120
for the loss of his family.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:57.215
As such, it looks like Dom's own family will
be the prime targets of the villain's revenge plot.

00:00:57.215 --> 00:01:03.320
One particularly alarming shot of the trailer
sees Dom's son Brian once again getting kidnapped.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.765
"That's the problem with having such a big
family.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:09.861
How do you choose the ones you save?"

00:01:10.544 --> 00:01:16.880
And speaking of Dante, he tends to steal the
show with his outrageous and vindictive behavior.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:22.070
From the very first moments of his appearance
and voice over, one can tell that this new

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:23.740
antagonist means business.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:28.560
But it might not be just business that brings
this new character into Dom's life.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.850
It seems as if this Dante character is actually
connected to events from "Fast Five," and

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:39.120
may actually be related to the villain of
that movie, the politician and drug-lord Hernan

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.700
Reyes in some form.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:46.450
Based on some interview comments, it seems
like he might be the son of that past antagonist.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:51.130
Speaking with Variety, Momoa explained how
much he enjoyed working on "Fast X" and his

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.530
time as a villain by saying,

00:01:52.644 --> 00:01:53.934
"Time of my life.

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:55.808
I get to be the bad guy finally.

00:01:55.808 --> 00:01:57.770
I've been the good guy for a while.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:02.980
[Dante's] very sadistic and androgynous and
he's a bit of a peacock...

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:04.515
He's got a lot of issues, this guy.

00:02:04.515 --> 00:02:07.135
He's definitely got some daddy issues."

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:13.459
In a twist that surprises no one, "Fast X"
adds yet another villain-turned-ally to the

00:02:13.459 --> 00:02:18.280
Fast Saga, with John Cena's Jakob Toretto
officially joining the family.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:22.480
While we only get a brief look at Dom and
Jakob's new relationship, it's worth noting

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:26.480
that Jakob's tone indicates the brothers are
on good terms after making amends at the end

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:27.530
of "F9."

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:31.230
Fans also get a look at Jakob taking on a
group of tactical soldiers.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:36.170
After combing through the shots of the trailer,
it seems that someone, presumably Dante, sent

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.610
the soldiers after Mia and Brian, Dom's son,
but Jakob comes to the rescue.

00:02:40.957 --> 00:02:45.670
With Brie Larson and Jason Momoa joining the
"Fast and Furious" franchise, it's easy to

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:49.909
overlook the first appearance of Alan Ritchson
as Agent Rimes.

00:02:49.909 --> 00:02:53.930
The trailer shows him getting ready to perform
some tactical shooting, but it's unclear who

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.200
his targets are.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:03:00.360
Momoa is obviously the Big Bad, but the film's
heroes have been known to rub law enforcement

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:01.840
the wrong way in the past.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:05.140
Will they get into it with Rimes, or will
he help them stop the bad guys?

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:10.560
If the history of this franchise tells us
anything, it's likely that both scenarios

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:11.560
will happen.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:15.400
Based on the little glimpse we’ve seen of
Rimes so far, it seems that the character

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.440
will fill a Hobbs-type role.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.750
The absence of Dwayne Johnson's no-nonsense
agent has left a void in the franchise that

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:26.220
still hasn't been filled yet, but Ritchson
is a solid choice to lead the next wave of

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.330
highly-trained cops into action.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:32.530
Furthermore, the "Jack Reacher" star is more
than capable of playing a convincing action

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:35.722
hero, so he should feel right at home in this
franchise already.

00:03:36.069 --> 00:03:41.760
If there's one thing that's become as consistent
with the "Fast and Furious" franchise as cars

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:46.849
and Coronas, it's old enemies patching things
up and clinking bottles by the end of a heavily

00:03:46.849 --> 00:03:48.150
fuelled installment.

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:52.870
Somehow, we managed to move on from the Shaw
brothers, Owen and Deckard, battling against

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:56.989
Dom and his family when they saved his son
in "The Fate of the Furious."

00:03:56.989 --> 00:04:01.689
With that said, the air is still in need of
clearing between two of the franchise's most

00:04:01.689 --> 00:04:03.140
iconic characters.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:07.300
Besides playing it safe with plenty of nods
back to previous films, one of the biggest

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:10.049
takeaways is seeing Deckard and Han sharing
the screen.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:14.510
They may look to be on speaking terms here,
but the chances of them getting in a scrap

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:19.019
to let off some long overdue steam beforehand
has to happen, right?

00:04:19.019 --> 00:04:23.240
The people have waited too long for justice
for Han, and now we might be getting it.

00:04:23.843 --> 00:04:29.740
For a saga that has never once attempted to
hide its most bonkers story choices, the tale

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:34.870
of Toretto has done the unthinkable in the
final moments of this new trailer — it actually

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:38.370
has stumped us over what's going on between
Letty and Cipher.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:42.979
If Dom playing tug of war with some helicopters
had our jaws dropping, seeing the long-time

00:04:42.979 --> 00:04:47.509
villain wake up with Dominic's sweetheart
has us scratching our chins and reaching a

00:04:47.509 --> 00:04:48.509
shocking theory.

00:04:48.509 --> 00:04:51.320
Are they...are they about to do a body swap?

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:57.212
It's become an unwritten rule after "Fast
Five" that anything could happen in this science-defying series.

00:04:57.212 --> 00:05:01.509
We thought it reached a limit for a franchise
that has sent two of its characters to space

00:05:01.509 --> 00:05:06.039
in a clapped-out Pontiac Fiero, as well as
revealing our leading man had a brother he

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:08.620
didn't mention for nine films.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:13.810
And yet, something about those final few seconds
screams, "Face/Off," with both characters

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:17.449
appearing like they're looking in a mirror,
only...not.

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:19.460
Is this really what's happening?

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.603
Or is this theory simply…

00:05:21.603 --> 00:05:22.830
Ludacris?

00:05:24.292 --> 00:05:25.292
"Maybe.

00:05:25.945 --> 00:05:27.606
Or maybe you're just a dumba**."

00:05:28.756 --> 00:05:29.805
We can only wait and see.

